# No trailing slash. `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY only, so it does not
# match `node_modules` committed as a SYMLINK (git mode 120000, which git
# classifies as a file). That gap is why the symlink has been committed twice:
# a worktree that symlinks node_modules at the parent checkout, plus a
# `git add -A`, and nothing stopped it. Bare `node_modules` covers both forms.
node_modules
dist/
.env
.env.local
